<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rumbula massacre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1941">1941</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rumbula massacre was the killing of about 25,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> in Rumbula forest near Riga on 30 November and 8 December 1941. Most victims came from the Riga ghetto, together with about a thousand Jews deported from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, and were shot by Einsatzgruppe A under Friedrich Jeckeln with Latvian auxiliaries of the Arājs Kommando. It was one of the largest mass shootings of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rumbula-massacre.jpg" alt="Rumbula massacre" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adam Jones · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Memorial_Marker_-_Rumbula_Forest_Holocaust_Site_-_Riga_-_Latvia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
